From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:56:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LvglLib: Build LVGL v9.6

LvglPkg builds LVGL v9.5.0, the commit of its submodule. ouroBIOS takes
LVGL v9.6, the last release of v9, at the head of its release/v9.6
branch (tools/build.sh, LVGL_COMMIT: v9.6.0 and the fixes after it).
v9.6.0 has the fix of the circle mask that 0016 took from it, so 0016
is gone. What LvglLib needs for v9.6:

- LvglLib.inf: v9.6 moved 49 of the sources that the library lists
  (fs/, image/, font/, logging/, debugging/profiler/, the MIPI display
  drivers, the Wayland driver), removed three (the QR code and barcode
  libraries, now widgets, and a stub) and added 23. The list stays
  every .c file of src/ but the three UEFI input drivers of LVGL, which
  lv_port_indev.c replaces.
- lv_conf.h: an option that v9.6 renamed gives a #warning, an error
  with -Werror. LV_COLOR_FORMAT_DEFAULT XRGB8888 in place of
  LV_COLOR_DEPTH 32 (the same format); LV_ASSERT_HANDLER_INCLUDE
  (<stdint.h>, which the handler does not need) out; the day and month
  names of the calendar from LV_SUNDAY_STR... and LV_JANUARY_STR...,
  the same strings. v9.6 turns LV_ASSERT() and LV_ASSERT_MSG() off by
  default: LV_USE_ASSERT 1 keeps them, as in v9.5. LV_PROFILER_INCLUDE
  follows the header (the profiler is off).
- v9.6 deprecates the flag API, lv_obj_add_flag() and the others, which
  lv_port_indev.c and the display engine call 54 times; v10 removes it.
  -Wno-deprecated-declarations in LvglLib.inf and
  LvglDisplayEngineDxe.inf, until the code moves to the setters of v9.6
  (lv_obj_set_hidden() and the others).

LvglDisplayEngine.efi is 598016 bytes, 577536 with v9.5.0 (LZMA, as in
the firmware volume: 244920 and 236344).

TEST=LvglPkg.dsc builds with GCC -Werror (RELEASE, X64) and no warning.
